    'Check the links that point at your own sites. A link to a page one of your elements or routes answers for is settled out of the database rather than over HTTP, because asking your own server about a page it just rendered is a request paid for twice. Anything the database cannot account for is asked for over HTTP like any other link, so a redirect rule, a rewrite or a file gets an honest answer instead of being called broken. Turn this off and links to your own sites are left out of the reports altogether.' => 'Check the links that point at your own sites. A link to a page one of your elements or routes answers for is settled out of the database rather than over HTTP, because asking your own server about a page it just rendered is a request paid for twice. Anything the database cannot account for is asked for over HTTP like any other link, so a redirect rule, a rewrite or a file gets an honest answer instead of being called broken. Turn this off and links to your own sites are left out of the reports altogether.',
