    'Fetch each of your own pages over HTTP and read the links out of the HTML a visitor actually gets. This is the only way to catch what a template hard-codes: the footer, the main nav, the widget somebody dropped into a layout years ago. None of that is in anybody\'s content, so nothing else in a scan will ever see it. It costs one request per page against your own server, so keep the page cap sensible and leave this off if your site is very large or the server is tight.' => 'Fetch each of your own pages over HTTP and read the links out of the HTML a visitor actually gets. This is the only way to catch what a template hard-codes: the footer, the main nav, the widget somebody dropped into a layout years ago. None of that is in anybody\'s content, so nothing else in a scan will ever see it. It costs one request per page against your own server, so keep the page cap sensible and leave this off if your site is very large or the server is tight.',
