    'Somebody decided these do not need reporting. They are left out of every other list and never checked again, and the decision holds through a full rescan. There is nothing to do here unless one of them needs watching again: Restore puts it back on the lists and checks it there and then. URLs quieted by an ignore rule in the settings are not listed here, those are edited in the settings.' => 'Somebody decided these do not need reporting. They are left out of every other list and never checked again, and the decision holds through a full rescan. There is nothing to do here unless one of them needs watching again: Restore puts it back on the lists and checks it there and then. URLs quieted by an ignore rule in the settings are not listed here, those are edited in the settings.',
    'Somebody decided this one does not need checking.' => 'Somebody decided this one does not need checking.',
    'Somebody who has since left' => 'Somebody who has since left',
    'Stage' => 'Stage',
    'Stop the scan? Everything it has already checked stays on the report, and the content it never reached is read by the next scan.' => 'Stop the scan? Everything it has already checked stays on the report, and the content it never reached is read by the next scan.',
    'Stop this scan' => 'Stop this scan',
    'Stopped' => 'Stopped',
    'Strip Tracking Parameters' => 'Strip Tracking Parameters',
    'Take the tour' => 'Take the tour',
    'Take utm_source, fbclid, gclid and the rest off a URL before it is stored, so the same link shared with three campaign tags is one URL and one request rather than three.' => 'Take utm_source, fbclid, gclid and the rest off a URL before it is stored, so the same link shared with three campaign tags is one URL and one request rather than three.',
    'Taking it again' => 'Taking it again',
    'Technical Detail' => 'Technical Detail',
    'Temporary' => 'Temporary',
    'Temporary only' => 'Temporary only',
    'That URL is ignored, so it is not checked. Restore it first.' => 'That URL is ignored, so it is not checked. Restore it first.',
    'That URL was not ignored.' => 'That URL was not ignored.',
    'That URL will not be reported again until somebody restores it.' => 'That URL will not be reported again until somebody restores it.',
    'That did not work. Try again.' => 'That did not work. Try again.',
    'That is the lot. This link brings the tour back any time.' => 'That is the lot. This link brings the tour back any time.',
    'The ceiling on how many pages one crawl fetches. Pages are taken in a fixed order and whatever is left over is named in the log, so a crawl that stops short says so rather than quietly handing you a report that looks complete.' => 'The ceiling on how many pages one crawl fetches. Pages are taken in a fixed order and whatever is left over is named in the log, so a crawl that stops short says so rather than quietly handing you a report that looks complete.',
    'The host asked to be left alone for a while, so nothing was checked. Try again shortly.' => 'The host asked to be left alone for a while, so nothing was checked. Try again shortly.',
    'The host asked us to ease off' => 'The host asked us to ease off',
    'The hosts and pages carrying the most broken links. Start here when there is a lot to do: fixing one page often clears several.' => 'The hosts and pages carrying the most broken links. Start here when there is a lot to do: fixing one page often clears several.',
    'The incoming webhook URL from your Slack app. Anybody holding this URL can post into your channel, so keep it in an environment variable rather than typing it in here: settings are stored in project config, which is committed. Type $ to see what is available.' => 'The incoming webhook URL from your Slack app. Anybody holding this URL can post into your channel, so keep it in an environment variable rather than typing it in here: settings are stored in project config, which is committed. Type $ to see what is available.',
    'The least time left between two requests to the same host, in milliseconds. A host that answers with a 429, the code for "you are asking too often", raises its own gap from there.' => 'The least time left between two requests to the same host, in milliseconds. A host that answers with a 429, the code for "you are asking too often", raises its own gap from there.',
    'The link scan on {site} has finished, and {count, plural, =1{one broken link came} other{# broken links came}} out of it.' => 'The link scan on {site} has finished, and {count, plural, =1{one broken link came} other{# broken links came}} out of it.',
    'The lists' => 'The lists',
    'The lists live here. The numbers beside them are live counts for the site you are on.' => 'The lists live here. The numbers beside them are live counts for the site you are on.',
    'The message as it arrived' => 'The message as it arrived',
    'The note after each link is what the website said when it was asked. The full list, and the pages carrying each one, is here: {url}' => 'The note after each link is what the website said when it was asked. The full list, and the pages carrying each one, is here: {url}',
    'The pages these links point at have moved for good, and your content still carries the old addresses. The links still work, but they are worth updating.' => 'The pages these links point at have moved for good, and your content still carries the old addresses. The links still work, but they are worth updating.',
    'The same, for a link that redirects somewhere that answers.' => 'The same, for a link that redirects somewhere that answers.',
    'The scan has been stopped. Everything it checked before it stopped is on the report as normal, and the next scan reads the rest.' => 'The scan has been stopped. Everything it checked before it stopped is on the report as normal, and the next scan reads the rest.',
    'The scan has started. The counts on this page will fill in as it works through your content.' => 'The scan has started. The counts on this page will fill in as it works through your content.',
    'The server answered with an error' => 'The server answered with an error',
    'The server asked to be asked less often' => 'The server asked to be asked less often',
    'The server could not make sense of the request' => 'The server could not make sense of the request',
    'The server could not take the request just then' => 'The server could not take the request just then',
    'The server had a problem' => 'The server had a problem',
    'The server hit an error of its own' => 'The server hit an error of its own',
    'The server refused it or could not find it' => 'The server refused it or could not find it',
    'The server refused the request' => 'The server refused the request',
    'The way to run this on a schedule is cron. It runs when you say it runs, it leaves a log, and it does not depend on anybody visiting the site. A nightly incremental scan reads only what has changed since the last one, and the checking is incremental for free, because a verdict is only asked again once it has gone stale.' => 'The way to run this on a schedule is cron. It runs when you say it runs, it leaves a log, and it does not depend on anybody visiting the site. A nightly incremental scan reads only what has changed since the last one, and the checking is incremental for free, because a verdict is only asked again once it has gone stale.',
    'These all still work, so nobody is landing on an error. A permanent one is worth tidying up anyway: the page it points at has moved for good and your content is still carrying the old address. Copy what is in the Goes To column into the link and it stops being a detour.' => 'These all still work, so nobody is landing on an error. A permanent one is worth tidying up anyway: the page it points at has moved for good and your content is still carrying the old address. Copy what is in the Goes To column into the link and it stops being a detour.',
    'These are gone. The website answered with a 404 or a 410, the codes for a page that is not there any more, or the link failed enough times in a row to be counted as gone. Each one is a link somebody clicks and lands nowhere, so put the right address in or take the link out.' => 'These are gone. The website answered with a 404 or a 410, the codes for a page that is not there any more, or the link failed enough times in a row to be counted as gone. Each one is a link somebody clicks and lands nowhere, so put the right address in or take the link out.',
    'These are not broken. The websites they point at refuse to answer anything but a person in a browser, so the checker cannot get an honest answer out of them. Plenty of big sites do this. There is usually nothing to fix here: open one in a new tab, and if the page comes up, leave the link alone.' => 'These are not broken. The websites they point at refuse to answer anything but a person in a browser, so the checker cannot get an honest answer out of them. Plenty of big sites do this. There is usually nothing to fix here: open one in a new tab, and if the page comes up, leave the link alone.',
    'These are policy, not decisions about one link. A rule written here is applied to everything that matches it, before and after, and it takes a URL out of the checking entirely. Dismissing a single broken link is a different thing, done from the lists themselves, and those dismissals are listed on the Ignored screen with the name and the date on them.' => 'These are policy, not decisions about one link. A rule written here is applied to everything that matches it, before and after, and it takes a URL out of the checking entirely. Dismissing a single broken link is a different thing, done from the lists themselves, and those dismissals are listed on the Ignored screen with the name and the date on them.',
    'These are the manners the checker goes out with. The defaults are set to be a good guest on somebody else\'s server: a handful of requests at a time, never more than two at any one host, and a gap between them. Raising them speeds a scan up and makes it look more like an attack, so raise them slowly and watch what comes back.' => 'These are the manners the checker goes out with. The defaults are set to be a good guest on somebody else\'s server: a handful of requests at a time, never more than two at any one host, and a gap between them. Raising them speeds a scan up and makes it look more like an attack, so raise them slowly and watch what comes back.',
    'These did not answer when last checked: a server that was down, or an address that would not resolve. They are retried on their own, and one that keeps failing is called Broken after a few failures in a row.' => 'These did not answer when last checked: a server that was down, or an address that would not resolve. They are retried on their own, and one that keeps failing is called Broken after a few failures in a row.',
    'These did not answer when they were asked: a server that was down or an address that would not resolve. They are tried again on their own, and one that keeps failing moves to Broken. Nothing to do here unless you already know a link is wrong.' => 'These did not answer when they were asked: a server that was down or an address that would not resolve. They are tried again on their own, and one that keeps failing moves to Broken. Nothing to do here unless you already know a link is wrong.',
    'These refused an automated check. LinkedIn and sites behind Cloudflare are the usual ones. They are most likely grand in a real browser, so they are never counted as broken.' => 'These refused an automated check. LinkedIn and sites behind Cloudflare are the usual ones. They are most likely grand in a real browser, so they are never counted as broken.',
    'This one is being left alone. It is kept out of every list and never checked, until somebody puts it back.' => 'This one is being left alone. It is kept out of every list and never checked, until somebody puts it back.',
    'This run was stopped before it finished. The counts cover what it got through.' => 'This run was stopped before it finished. The counts cover what it got through.',
    'Those settings could not be saved. Check the fields marked below and try again.' => 'Those settings could not be saved. Check the fields marked below and try again.',
    'Tick what a scan should read. Out of the box that is entries, categories, tags and global sets, plus Commerce products and variants. Everything else stays out until you tick it here, orders and users included: there are an awful lot of them and no editor ever typed a link into one. Untick the lot and a scan reads nothing at all.' => 'Tick what a scan should read. Out of the box that is entries, categories, tags and global sets, plus Commerce products and variants. Everything else stays out until you tick it here, orders and users included: there are an awful lot of them and no editor ever typed a link into one. Untick the lot and a scan reads nothing at all.',
